'' A function-like macro name that ENDS an expansion frame must not eat the token
'' after it. Deciding whether a '(' follows used to Advance first and restore f->pos
'' on a miss; when the name was the frame's last token, PeekTok's pop cascade had
'' already deleted that frame, so the restore wrote into a popped slot and PpStep
'' then advanced -- and discarded -- the token from the ENCLOSING frame. Silent: the
'' program simply lost a token. See PeekTokAhead in src/pp/pp.bas.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc 1.10.1 -pp on tests/pp/src/macro-bare-lookahead.bas:
''
''      fn aaa
''
''      100 + 777 bbb
''
''      ccc
''
''     dim s as string = $"o" + letter  ddd
''
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-tokens=pp tests/pp/src/macro-bare-lookahead.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' 1. 'fn' bare, and the token it used to swallow.
'' EXPECT-OUT: IDENT               'fn'
'' EXPECT-OUT: IDENT               'aaa'

'' 2. the invocation across the frame boundary still happens -- 'takes' is consumed,
''    not emitted -- and 'bbb' after the ')' is still there.
'' EXPECT-NOT: IDENT               'takes'
'' EXPECT-OUT: IDENT               'bbb'

'' 3. the '?' form is still a bare invocation: 'opt' goes, its argument comes back.
'' EXPECT-NOT: IDENT               'opt'
'' EXPECT-OUT: IDENT               'ccc'

'' 4. hidden 'letter' is emitted as an identifier, 'ddd' behind it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: IDENT               'letter'
'' EXPECT-OUT: IDENT               'ddd'
